=== POST-HOC ANNOTATIONS (dev box, 2026-09-10, not part of capture) ===
1. Netcon echo duplication: operator keystrokes appear garbled/doubled in the
   UDP capture (e.g. "XHCI-RESEE T", "PHYS-AUDi IT"). The machine received
   clean input in every case -- responses are plain "ok", never "?" -- so this
   is a capture-side echo artifact, not machine input corruption.
2. Signed hex rendering: "-4EDE7B94" (the XECP-FIND cap address before the
   LEGCTL read) is the signed rendering of 0xB121846C -- inside BAR
   0xB1210000. Not a fault.
3. Card bug found in-trip: Section 2 gate uses DEF? but DEF? is a suite-side
   runtime definition, not a kernel word. The two aborted "DEF? ?" lines
   popped one cell off the empty stack (DEPTH read 1073741823 = -1 cell).
   Repair on iron: pushed a single 0, DEPTH then read 0; all subsequent
   lines balanced. Card fixed post-trip to include ": DEF? WORD FIND NIP ;".
4. Settled readings (re-derived from this log):
   OWNER=1 -> CLAIM=-1 (outcome B, BIOS yielded in-budget)
   LEGCTL before: 0x40002000 (bit 13 ownership-change SMI enable armed,
     bit 30 RW1C status latched); SMI-OFF=1 (write occurred and stuck)
   MEMDISK-BASE@ = 0x37BB7000, low-12 = 0 (gate PASS, matches 09-05)
   Pre-halt HCH=1 (BIOS quiesced controller on yield; inverts QEMU/SeaBIOS)
   XHCI-RESET -1, HCRST 1 ms, CNR 0 ms (1000 ms budget -> measurement)
   NOP-TEST 32/32 (ring wrapped twice, link-toggle executed on iron)
   Survey #1 -> #2: PED cleared + CSC latched on occupied ports (2d
     mechanism on iron); ports 13-18 latched WRC (bit 19) = USB3 bank
   XHCI-DOWN -1; PHYS-AUDIT unattributed: 0 (clean)

=== CORRECTION (2026-09-10, post-review) ===
Annotation 4's line "Pre-halt HCH=1 (BIOS quiesced controller on
yield)" overstates. HCH was read ONCE, at Section 5 -- AFTER the
claim. The log does not determine whether the controller was already
halted at boot or halted in response to the handoff. Corrected
statement: post-claim the controller read halted, which inverts what
SeaBIOS does; mechanism undetermined by this log. A pre-claim HCH
reading next trip settles it.

=== CORRECTION 2 (2026-09-10, post-review) ===
Annotation 3 is wrong in two ways, and misses the real finding.
(a) Only the SECOND gate line (17:43:00) underflowed -- its "." popped
one cell off the empty stack, printing -1900006918. The FIRST line
(17:42:51) was balanced: "DEF? ?" aborted DEF?, but XHCI-CLAIM *is*
defined and EXECUTED -- the "0 ok" on that line is XHCI-CLAIM's own
return value, printed by the trailing ".".
(b) The finding: XHCI-CLAIM ran BEFORE XHCI-BIND (17:44:02), against
XHCI-BASE = 0. HCC1 then reads address 0x10 -- the real-mode IVT. On
this machine bits 31:16 of that read came back zero, so XECP-BASE
exited early and the word returned 0 harmlessly. Had those bits been
nonzero, a cap-ID match would have sent (CLAIM) into a WRITE
("DUP @ 1000000 OR OVER !") against a low-memory address. XHCI-CLAIM,
SMI-OFF, XECP-FIND and XECP-BASE all derive addresses from XHCI-BASE
with no bound check -- same fail-open shape PORTSC-ADDR was guarded
against in 2d, except this one can write. Guard + refusal test =
carried debt into step 3 (see closure doc).
